# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# REAL CUSTOMER DATA — NEVER COMMIT
#
# This project processes RBL Bank cardholder records: full names, mobile numbers,
# 19-digit card account numbers, outstanding balances, and delinquency status.
# Publishing that — even to a private repo, even to Vercel — is a personal-data
# breach under India's DPDP Act, and it is the bank's customers who pay for it.
#
# Everything below stays on the machine that produced it. Nothing here is needed
# to run the app: `npm run demo` generates a synthetic book with invented people.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# raw exports and anything derived from them
*.csv
*.tsv
!evals/upload/4_SYNTHETIC_10k_inverted_book.csv     # invented people, safe to share

# the local data store: source CSV, canonical rows, explorer rows, batch payloads.
# Note the trailing /* — git cannot un-ignore a file inside an EXCLUDED DIRECTORY,
# so we exclude the contents and then re-admit the one safe file.
/src/data/*
# ...except the model's measured credentials. Aggregate statistics only — no
# account, no name, no rupee figure tied to a person. The app imports it at build,
# so if this is missing the Vercel build fails.
!/src/data/validation.json

# eval artefacts built from the real book
/evals/reports/
/evals/upload/
/evals/sweep/
/evals/cases.jsonl
/evals/llm_blind.jsonl
/evals/llm_preds.json
/evals/model_card.json
/evals/stress_report.json
/evals/stress_merge_report.txt
/evals/llm_sweep_results.json

# rendered slides (contain client figures)
/deck/*.pdf
/deck/slide-*.jpg

# Early HTML prototypes with REAL cardholder rows baked into the markup —
# 31 card numbers and 6 mobiles sitting in plain text at the repo root.
# Ignored here; delete them from disk when you get a chance, they serve no purpose.
/dashboard_preview.html
/.preview_body.html
*_preview.html


# The public tunnel URL, written by `npm run dev`. Ephemeral, and pointing at a
# machine — never commit it.
.tunnel-url
FEATURE_PROMPT.md
